From 2519d35c78e7ba0b3953efe5c1f910f9f3af4c15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] r4 sky-dome fix: dome follows the board clear colour per
 mode, straight sRGB line (no lavender detour)

Lead rejected 939049c's dome target (waterSky* zenith/low = water-only
reflection colours, pre-compensated for the water tint; it routed the day
dome through lavender). The dome/cloud target is again the sky the board
shows: lakesideSkyDomeColor(mode) = hexRgb(lakesideModeLighting(mode).clearColor)
(day 28/143/184 = lakesideDayClearColor), one small accessor to repoint when
Voice Bot exports a per-mode skyDomeColor. Read-only, no waterSky* on the dome.
skyFollowColor now moves the shown average (mainColor x mesh average) along a
straight sRGB line from the island start to the target: every channel
monotonic and the hue moving one way between start and end (a linear-rgb lerp
bent the cloud layer's hue). w=0/1 unchanged (island base / target gain).
SKY_FOLLOW_MAX_GAIN back to 8 (clear-colour gains fit: max 1.93);
skyFollowTargetFromLinear removed.
Test lakeside-sky-follow: target = board clear per mode, accessor wiring, no
waterSky*, clamp 8, and 21-step blend 0..1 day + night on the real dome and
cloud averages: each channel monotonic within start..end, hue on the short
arc between start and end, never turning back.
